cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PET/MRI Longitudinal Analysis Template"
message: "If you use or adapt this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Chu"
    given-names: "Georgina W."
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3645-795X

abstract: >
  This repository provides a reproducible R/Quarto template for analyzing
  simulated longitudinal PET/MRI and cognitive data. It demonstrates
  simulated data organization, neuroimaging-style quality-control checks,
  paired longitudinal completeness checks, descriptive summaries,
  mixed-effects longitudinal modeling, within-person and between-person
  PET marker decomposition, change-score sensitivity analysis, and
  Quarto-based reporting. The repository uses simulated data only and does
  not contain real participant data, raw neuroimaging files, unpublished
  project materials, or collaborator-owned results.

keywords:
  - PET
  - MRI
  - neuroimaging
  - longitudinal analysis
  - cognitive neuroscience
  - mixed-effects models
  - quality control
  - reproducible research
  - Quarto
  - R

